WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.211
Secure IaC automation needs evidence.

2
00:00:03.291 --> 00:00:08.385
Teams should know who triggered a run,
which identity applied the change,

3
00:00:08.465 --> 00:00:13.477
which repository and commit were used,
which environment was targeted,

4
00:00:13.557 --> 00:00:17.501
what plan was reviewed, and whether the
apply succeeded.

5
00:00:17.581 --> 00:00:23.250
Without that evidence, it is difficult to
investigate failures, prove approval,

6
00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:27.603
or understand how the environment reached
its current state.

7
00:00:27.683 --> 00:00:31.873
Logs should be useful without exposing
sensitive material.

8
00:00:31.953 --> 00:00:37.294
They should record identity, commit,
environment, plan reference, action,

9
00:00:37.374 --> 00:00:39.181
and result at a safe level.

10
00:00:39.261 --> 00:00:43.451
They should avoid secrets, excessive
sensitive state data,

11
00:00:43.531 --> 00:00:48.050
endpoints or configuration details that do
not help operations,

12
00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:52.238
and raw outputs that could be copied into
broad log systems.

13
00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:56.591
Logs are often widely accessible and
retained for a long time.

14
00:00:56.671 --> 00:01:01.354
Monitoring should detect failed runs,
unexpected changes, drift,

15
00:01:01.434 --> 00:01:06.939
missing security controls, unusual
identities, repeated policy exceptions,

16
00:01:07.019 --> 00:01:09.073
and repeated apply failures.

17
00:01:09.153 --> 00:01:12.850
Drift can indicate manual changes,
automation gaps,

18
00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:15.642
or policy exceptions that need review.

19
00:01:15.722 --> 00:01:21.473
Monitoring should feed operational review
rather than sit unused until an audit or

20
00:01:21.553 --> 00:01:22.292
incident.

21
00:01:22.372 --> 00:01:28.206
Rollback planning matters because not
every infrastructure change can be safely or

22
00:01:28.286 --> 00:01:29.929
automatically undone.

23
00:01:30.009 --> 00:01:35.843
Some changes affect stateful resources,
identity, networking, or data retention.

24
00:01:35.923 --> 00:01:41.181
Incident response should include
containment, review of applied changes,

25
00:01:41.261 --> 00:01:46.684
credential review, state review, and
lessons learned for future guardrails.

26
00:01:46.764 --> 00:01:51.940
A failed or unauthorized IaC change should
make the next change path safer.
